<!--
  Twinkle Address: Alfred as Twinkle's address bar.

  ⌘L, only while Twinkle is in front, shows the script filter with nothing
  typed; twinkle-query (a link Twinkle keeps in its Application Support
  folder) lists the current page first, so typing replaces it and ⇥ puts it
  in the box to edit. Results come from history and open tabs; the choice
  goes back to Twinkle as a twinkle:// link. ↩ opens in the current tab, ⌘↩
  in a new one. The "address" external trigger (Twinkle's own ⌘L, if the
  hotkey is unset) and the "tw" keyword lead to the same place.
-->
